---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Agent-friendly hardware workbench: flash, monitor, and probe ESP32 boards

Usage: pogo [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  devices      List connected serial devices and classify them
  doctor       Check the environment: config, devices, permissions, probe
  info         Read chip, revision, features, MAC, and flash size (resets the target)
  flash        Flash an ELF or raw .bin image to the target
  reset        Reset the target into run mode or the bootloader
  serial       Capture and send serial data
  run          Flash, reset, and capture in one step (the main agent command)
  i2c          I2C bus access through the probe
  gpio         GPIO control through the probe
  power        Current measurement and power switching through the probe
  probe        Probe board information and self-test
  config       Inspect and validate configuration
  schema       Print the JSON Schema for a command's envelope
  completions  Print shell completions
  mcp          Start the MCP server on stdio
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

Every command terminates, writes results only to stdout, and returns a documented exit code.
Use -f json (or POGO_FORMAT=json) for one JSON envelope:
  { schema_version, pogo_version, command, ok, duration_ms, data, error, warnings }

Examples:
  pogo devices -f json
  pogo run app.elf --until READY --timeout 20s -f json

Exit codes:
  0 ok   1 internal/not implemented   2 usage   3 device not found/ambiguous
  4 timeout   5 permission denied   6 device I/O or probe protocol   7 target fault
  8 guardrail refused   9 device busy   10 config invalid   130 interrupted
